<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jogulamba Gadwal district</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Jogulamba Gadwal district is a district in the south of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/telangana">Telangana</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/krishna">Krishna</a> and Tungabhadra rivers, with its headquarters at Gadwal. It was formed in 2016 from part of Mahbubnagar district and is named after the goddess Jogulamba, whose temple at Alampur is counted among the Shakti Peethas. The town of Gadwal was the seat of the Gadwal Samasthan, a tributary state of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hyderabad">Hyderabad</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/jogulamba-gadwal-district.jpg" alt="Jogulamba Gadwal district" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ms Sarah Welch · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Vishwa_Brahma_(L)_and_Veera_Brahma_(R)_Temples,_Alampur,_Telangana_India.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
